From 9273e785680eb9397ea6f094d748f412790cc798 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:50:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: soft: Select the colour correction by lux index

The vendor tuning keys its colour correction matrices by lux index as
well as colour temperature, and the soft IPA used the one region, for
every light. Give Agc a model of the lux index (lux: refProduct,
perStop): the exposure time x gain that brings the frame to the luma
target, in stops from that of lux index 250. Ccm takes luxSets, the
matrices by lux index region, and blends the two regions either side of
a gap in the tuning's ranges, as CamX interpolates. Without luxSets or
the model, ccms apply as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
